Mice were head-mounted above a cylindrical treadmill and calcium imaging was performed using Chameleon Ti-Sapphire laser (Coherent) tuned to 920 nm and a large FOV mesoscope67 equipped with a custom objective (excitation NA 0.6, collection NA 1.0, 21 mm focal length). Laser power after the objective was increased exponentially as a function of depth from the surface according to: \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
